just a short time ago the White House  announced the president tested negative  for kovat 19 after coming in contact  with a Brazilian official who was  infected  let's bring in former White House  physician and a congressional candidate  dr. Ronnie Jackson also a retired Navy  Rear Admiral  dr. Jackson thanks very much for being  with us given what happened with given  with the what happened with the  Brazilian delegation and with the press  secretary from Brazil's presidential  office testing positive for coronavirus  was it appropriate for president Trump  to take that test  well John I'll tell you you know I think  the president's trying to you know abide  by the same rules that we're going to  apply to everybody else in this country  with regards to testing and be honest  with you I don't think there was a  clinical indication for to get a test I  think that it was much like the  situation that I was in if you remember  back when I did his his physical exam  his first physical exam and I did the  cognitive testing there was no  indication for the cognitive testing  either but there comes a point where the  narrative is all about just that and you  have to do something just to move on to  whatever's next and actually put it to  bed and I think that's pretty much what  happened here I don't think there was a  clinical indication to do the test I  think that they looked at the weather  where the president failed with regards  to risk based on these exposures and I  think that what they ultimately decided  and I think the president had a big role  in this just like he did when I did the  cognitive testing he just said hey let's  just do the test let's get this over  with let's put it to bed and let's move  on I mean he's working hard to try to  take care of our country here and keep  us all safe and I think you know the the  press some of the liberal press and  those on the Left are really spun this  up and we have other things we need to  move on and focus on so I'm glad that he  got the test done I'm glad that it's  negative and I hope that we can move on  down and it's not trying to make  political hay just carry on we just put  up some of the bullet points of the  contents contents of this family's first  coronavirus respond response act and  there they are again  is there anything else that that you  think should be in the legislation well  I can't see I can't see what you have on  the screen there but I mean I think that  the legislation is good based on what I  know about it what I've read I think  that there's probably stuff in there you  know  it was forced to now think you know  that's kind of what upsets me as just an  American here is that sometimes they're  there folks that are using the crisis  like this for political advantage and to  get things into legislation that maybe  shouldn't be in there that don't  necessarily address the problem so I'd  have to look at everything but I think  from what I've heard with the testing  and the access and things of that nature  I think it's probably appropriate I'm  sure the president wouldn't have you  know signed off on it it had not been  something that's that's appropriate for  facing the president also has declared a  national emergency I want to play for  you now some of the reasons that he said  he decided to do that listen yesterday I  declared a national emergency which was  a very big deal because it opened up  avenues that we would never be able to  open up without it it'll make more than  50 billion dollars available to us  immediately in disaster relief funds I'm  still struck by how much life is  changing in this country as a result of  this virus that although it has killed  some people it's a relatively small  number and primarily elderly people and  people who were you know had underlying  medical conditions in a couple of weeks  in a month are we gonna look back on  this and say you know we went overboard  on this do you think dr. Jackson or are  these steps simply prudent well you know  these steps are proven because we just  don't know but I hope you're right and I  think you are right I think we will look  back on this and instead we overreacted  a little bit I guess it's better to be  safe than sorry you know in some regards  but you know I think that this thing's  been spun for political reasons and I  think that a lot of people have really  gone overboard with it just you know and  it created a lot of fear that doesn't  need to be there I mean I'm telling you  I'm talking to here from Amarillo Texas  and I just went to a Saint Patrick's Day  parade and shamrock Texas this morning  and folks here not getting too spun up  about it you know they're out there and  you know there weren't a lot of elderly  people out there so people are  protecting their grandparents and their  elderly parents making sure they stay  home and they bring groceries to them  and do things like that but the rest of  us that are young and otherwise healthy  we're getting out or not letting this  really just destroy our lives and it's  having a big impact on the economy and  we need to be able to get out and be  together to some extent we're taking  Prakash  we're washing our hands there's a lot of  sanity hand sanitizer out there things  of that nature but I think that we will  look back on this John and we will see  that this was a little bit overblown or  quite a bit overblown hopefully and  we'll be able to move on and do better  next time yeah when you look at the  store shelves that have been cleaned out  you look at the the athletic seasons  competitions that have been cancelled  universities that are canceling classes  to me it's it's unbelievable what is  happening as a result John's buyers  quickly yes I would say if you look at  this potentially going on for weeks and  weeks we can't sustain something like  that so we need to figure out how to how  to take a reasonable approach to this  and I think we we've gone a little bit  too far too fast with the cancellations  and the things that that nature the  president is working really hard with a  really great team to protect us and we  need to trust him to do that  unfortunately in this litigious society  people don't want to be held responsible  for you know getting this thing to turn  around dr. Ronnie Jackson it's good to  have you on thank you
 

